From 0b0d1e3b3548d4c7c174e312caae704af13db354 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Edwards <jeff@edwardsj.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:05:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] entropy: seed from virtio-rng and fail closed without a
 source

aarch64 has no seed_entropy(), so sys_read_entropy fell back to a 31-bit
Park-Miller-Lehmer generator seeded from the boot timer: guessable bytes
behind an interface that promises cryptographically secure ones. Add a
virtio entropy (virtio-rng) PCI driver behind the virtio-rng feature, seed
the ChaCha pool from it when the processor offers nothing, and return the
error instead of the weak bytes when there is no source at all. smoltcp's
seed (TCP initial sequence numbers, ephemeral ports) now comes from the
pool too, with the wall clock only as a logged last resort.
---
